From ced405d6c37c15bec5db8b79a3cbc9cff0e45270 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrija Panic <andrija.panic@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:40:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] convert_windows: check for a pending reboot in the 64-bit
 registry

Before installing the virtio drivers, the "pnputil install drivers"
firstboot script checks whether Windows is waiting for a restart to
finish installing updates, and if so retries after the next reboot
(exit 249).  It looks in three places: the Windows Update
RebootRequired key, the CBS (component servicing) RebootPending key and
the Session Manager PendingFileRenameOperations value.

The script runs under the firstboot service, which is the 32-bit
rhsrvany.exe; that is also why it calls %systemroot%\Sysnative\PnPutil.
Its reg.exe is therefore 32-bit too, and on 64-bit Windows a 32-bit
"reg query HKLM\SOFTWARE\..." is redirected to WOW6432Node.  The
Windows Update and CBS checks never see the real keys, and only the
PendingFileRenameOperations check (HKLM\SYSTEM is not redirected)
works.  A guest converted with updates still pending, for example a
server patched but not yet restarted, then runs pnputil while Windows
is still servicing, and since commit fe53f740 a driver that fails
there is reported instead of retried.

Use the 64-bit reg.exe through Sysnative when it exists, as the script
already does for PnPutil, and plain reg otherwise (32-bit Windows, where
there is no redirection).  All three queries use it, so the checks read
the same registry that Windows Update and CBS write.

With the checks working, a reboot that stays pending makes the script
exit 249 on every boot; libguestfs-common commit a5afb049 bounds that
to 3 attempts.

Fixes: https://github.com/libguestfs/virt-v2v/issues/210

Backport of upstream commit 6d6417ea310177611d4a0d7deac6511e1970dd37,
pull request https://github.com/libguestfs/virt-v2v/pull/211.  Applied
by hand: rhel-9.8 carries the script in the older "...\n\" string form,
so the upstream diff does not apply as is.  The generated script is the
same as upstream's.

Signed-off-by: Andrija Panic <andrija.panic@gmail.com>
---
 convert/convert_windows.ml | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/convert/convert_windows.ml b/convert/convert_windows.ml
index 6c8a6688..35693e49 100644
--- a/convert/convert_windows.ml
+++ b/convert/convert_windows.ml
@@ -401,19 +401,26 @@ let convert (g : G.guestfs) source inspect i_firmware
                      echo Installing drivers from %inf_dir%\n\
                      set REBOOT_PENDING=0\n\
                      \n\
-                     reg query \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\WindowsUpdate\\Auto Update\\RebootRequired\"\n\
+                     rem The first-boot service that runs this script is a 32-bit program, so\n\
+                     rem on 64-bit Windows a plain \"reg query HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\...\" would read\n\
+                     rem WOW6432Node and never see the keys below.  Use the 64-bit reg.exe\n\
+                     rem when there is one, as for PnPutil.\n\
+                     set REG=reg\n\
+                     if exist %systemroot%\\Sysnative\\reg.exe set REG=%systemroot%\\Sysnative\\reg.exe\n\
+                     \n\
+                     %REG% query \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\WindowsUpdate\\Auto Update\\RebootRequired\"\n\
                      if %errorlevel%==0 (\n\
                      echo Windows Update: Reboot required.\n\
                      set REBOOT_PENDING=1\n\
                      )\n\
                      \n\
-                     reg query \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Component Based Servicing\\RebootPending\"\n\
+                     %REG% query \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Component Based Servicing\\RebootPending\"\n\
                      if %errorlevel%==0 (\n\
                      echo CBS: Reboot required.\n\
                      set REBOOT_PENDING=1\n\
                      )\n\
                      \n\
-                     reg query \"HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Session Manager\" /v PendingFileRenameOperations\n\
+                     %REG% query \"HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Session Manager\" /v PendingFileRenameOperations\n\
                      if %errorlevel%==0 (\n\
                      echo Session Manager: Reboot required.\n\
                      set REBOOT_PENDING=1\n\
-- 
